Frappe 16.35 is the web framework under /usr/lib/frappe. Sites and
uploaded files live in /var/lib/frappe/sites. The web service listens
on 127.0.0.1:8000. Realtime uses 127.0.0.1:9000. MariaDB is local.
Redis is three private instances on Unix sockets:
redis@frappe-cache, redis@frappe-queue and redis@frappe-socketio.

ERPNext is a separate package. Other Frappe applications install the
same way, on top of this package.

1. Start MariaDB and the private Redis instances:

   systemctl enable --now mariadb redis@frappe-cache redis@frappe-queue redis@frappe-socketio

2. Create the first site. MariaDB root on this system authenticates
   through the local socket, so run the command as root.

   frappe new-site localhost \
     --admin-password 'choose-one' \
     --mariadb-root-username root \
     --db-root-password ''

   Add --install-app erpnext when that package is installed.

3. Start the application:

   systemctl enable --now frappe frappe-worker frappe-scheduler frappe-socketio

4. Open http://localhost:8000 and log in as Administrator.

To put nginx in front, install frappe-nginx and enable the site:

   ln -s ../sites-available/frappe.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/frappe.conf
   systemctl reload nginx
